# Committed defaults, read by Symfony in every environment.
#
# Keep this file lean. Docker compose reads it too when it substitutes compose.yaml, so any value left here silently
# satisfies the `${VAR:?...}` guards in compose.yaml that are meant to catch a variable an operator forgot — a
# development password would be accepted as a production one without a word. `composer dump-env prod` also bakes what
# is here into the production image as a fallback, where the same applies.
#
# A value belongs here only when it is right in EVERY environment. Everything else lives:
#
#   - in config/services.yaml, as `env(NAME): default`, when it is a constant with a sane fallback rather than
#     something a deployment sets (the mail display names, the pinned Stripe API version, the watermark tag);
#   - in `.env.local` for development, created from `.env.local.dist` by `make start`;
#   - in `.env.test` for the test suite, which does not read `.env.local` at all;
#   - in the orchestrator for production — Portainer's stack environment (see compose.yaml) or the
#     ConfigMap and SealedSecret under k8s/.

###> symfony/framework-bundle ###
# Overridden to `prod` by the image (Dockerfile) and by compose.yaml, which defaults it rather than reading this
# file, so the development value cannot follow the checkout into a deployment.
APP_ENV=dev
###< symfony/framework-bundle ###
